<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_section" style="--ltx-fg-color:#2E5AA8;">2  Background and Related Work</h2>

<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#2E5AA8;">2.1  Gated Delta Rule</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Linear attention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite> removes the softmax, so that attention
becomes a recurrence over a state <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{k}\times d_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{k}\times d_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math> per head,</p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}=S_{t-1}+k_{t}v_{t}^{\top},\qquad o_{t}=S_{t}^{\top}q_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}=S_{t-1}+k_{t}v_{t}^{\top},\qquad o_{t}=S_{t}^{\top}q_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The state replaces the key–value cache. It holds the whole past, does not grow with context, and is read
and written at every step.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Variants differ in how <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is modified before the new token is written
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>, <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>. We work with the gated delta rule
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>, which applies a data-dependent decay <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and removes the
component of the state along the current key before writing,</p>
<table id="S2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}=a_{t}\left(I-\beta_{t}k_{t}k_{t}^{\top}\right)S_{t-1}+\beta_{t}k_{t}v_{t}^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}=a_{t}\left(I-\beta_{t}k_{t}k_{t}^{\top}\right)S_{t-1}+\beta_{t}k_{t}v_{t}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">with write strength <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. The read-out is unchanged. Expanding Eq. <a href="#S2.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 2.1 Gated Delta Rule ‣ 2 Background and Related Work ‣ PACE: Periodic and Channel-Aligned Encodingof Four-Bit Recurrent States" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, every write is an
outer product,</p>
<table id="S2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}=a_{t}S_{t-1}+k_{t}u_{t}^{\top},\;\;u_{t}=\beta_{t}(v_{t}-a_{t}S_{t-1}^{\top}k_{t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}=a_{t}S_{t-1}+k_{t}u_{t}^{\top},\;\;u_{t}=\beta_{t}(v_{t}-a_{t}S_{t-1}^{\top}k_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where we call <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> the <em id="S2.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">delta value</em>, the part of <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> that the decayed state does not already
return for <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, scaled by <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#2E5AA8;">2.2  Chunk-wise Kernels</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Evaluating Eq. <a href="#S2.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 2.1 Gated Delta Rule ‣ 2 Background and Related Work ‣ PACE: Periodic and Channel-Aligned Encodingof Four-Bit Recurrent States" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> token by token is sequential and memory-bound. Chunk-wise kernels
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>, <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite> split the sequence into chunks of length <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and process each
chunk from the state at its start. Writing <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}=\prod_{j\leq i}a_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}=\prod_{j\leq i}a_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for the cumulative decay
within a chunk, the state after <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> tokens is</p>
<table id="S2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{C}=\alpha_{C}S_{0}+\sum_{i=1}^{C}\frac{\alpha_{C}}{\alpha_{i}}\,k_{i}u_{i}^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{C}=\alpha_{C}S_{0}+\sum_{i=1}^{C}\frac{\alpha_{C}}{\alpha_{i}}\,k_{i}u_{i}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the outputs follow from <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and the chunk’s own tokens by matrix multiplication. The delta values
<math id="S2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of Eq. <a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ 2.1 Gated Delta Rule ‣ 2 Background and Related Work ‣ PACE: Periodic and Channel-Aligned Encodingof Four-Bit Recurrent States" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> are obtained from a triangular solve over the chunk, so Eq. <a href="#S2.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ 2.2 Chunk-wise Kernels ‣ 2 Background and Related Work ‣ PACE: Periodic and Channel-Aligned Encodingof Four-Bit Recurrent States" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> is evaluated
with dense arithmetic rather than a loop. Only <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> are formed as tensors. The states at
positions inside the chunk are never written.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2610.29545v1/fig_axis.png" id="S2.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/129;" width="476" height="129" alt="Refer to caption">
