</figure>
<div id="S7.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">At the resident bits of DAMP INT4, PACE-4/8 with an int8 buffer scores above DAMP INT4 on every
backbone, with the largest difference on Qwen3.6-35B-A3B. With its mixed buffer, PACE-4/8 scores
higher than this variant on the three larger backbones and lower on Qwen3.5-4B. PACE-4 holds the
same resident bits as Q-Mamba DSQ and scores higher on every backbone.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#2E5AA8;">7.3  Ablations</h3>

<div id="S7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare state quantizers on Qwen3.5-4B and 27B, changing one component at a time, and report
IFEval with a <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="95\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95\%</annotation></semantics></math> interval on the paired difference to the full-precision state and perplexity on
WikiText-103 at <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32{,}768" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32,768</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32{,}768</annotation></semantics></math> tokens (Table <a href="#S7.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 7.3 Ablations ‣ 7 Results ‣ PACE: Periodic and Channel-Aligned Encodingof Four-Bit Recurrent States" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Groups along the key axis yield a lower perplexity than groups along the value axis at the
same width, with and without head allocation, and a higher IFEval score without it. Q-Mamba DSQ yields a higher perplexity than key-axis
groups at the same resident bits per value.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">At equal resident bits, head-level allocation yields a lower perplexity than DAMP INT4.</p>
</div>
