two axes opposite to the max/RMS ratio. The step size of a group follows its largest entry, which the tail statistics in
Figure <a href="#S2.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 2.2 Chunk-wise Kernels ‣ 2 Background and Related Work ‣ PACE: Periodic and Channel-Aligned Encodingof Four-Bit Recurrent States" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and Table <a href="#A3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix C State Statistics along the Two Axes ‣ PACE: Periodic and Channel-Aligned Encodingof Four-Bit Recurrent States" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> measure.</p>
