<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Integer Zero Point</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The affine grid needs a zero point, and storing it as a float means an entry that has decayed to zero
is rounded to a nonzero value at every rounding. We snap the zero point onto the payload grid and store it
as a <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>-bit code, so the side information is <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(16+b)/32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(16+b)/32</annotation></semantics></math> bits per value and a decayed entry rounds
to zero by construction. An affine <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>-bit group takes <math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.625" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4.625</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.625</annotation></semantics></math> bits per value and an <math id="A5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>-bit group
<math id="A5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8.75" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8.75</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8.75</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
